"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"DPAn-3\", \"(7Z,10Z,13Z,16Z,19Z)-docosapentaenoate\", \"omega-3-docosapentaenoic acid\", \"(7Z,10Z,13Z,16Z,19Z)-docosapentaenoic acid\"], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-9608444\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-9608444.5\"}], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Ac-PTGS2 dimer oxidises DPAn-3 to 17-HDPAn-3\", \"(7Z,10Z,13Z,16Z,19Z)-docosapentaenoate + O2 => 17-hydroperoxy-(7Z,10Z,13Z,15E,19Z)-docosapentaenoate\"], \"output\": [{\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 9027614, \"displayName\": \"17-HDPAn-3 [cytosol]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"17-HDPAn-3\", \"(7Z,10Z,13Z,15E,19Z)-17-hydroperoxydocosapentaenoate\", \"(7Z,10Z,13Z,15E,19Z)-17-hydroperoxydocosapentaenoic acid\", \"17-hydroperoxy-omega3-docosapentaenoic acid\", \"17-hydroperoxy-docosapentaenoic acid\"], \"producedByEvent\": [10323964], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-9027614\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-9027614.5\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"CFA\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 49646, \"displayName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"name\": [\"Canis familiaris\", \"Canis lupus familiaris\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"9615\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Canis familiaris\", \"stId\": \"R-CFA-9027607\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-CFA-9027607.1\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9990864, \"displayName\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\"}]}"
